    {
      "id": "p0166-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In everyday Japanese, the personal pronoun washi is strongly associated with older people and parts of western Japan. In Japanese entertainment, washi can also lend a very \"traditional Japanese culture\" vibe to samurai warriors, sumo wrestlers, etc. Some familiar washi users include:",
        "raw": "In everyday Japanese, the personal pronoun washi is strongly associated\nwith older people and parts of western Japan. In Japanese entertainment,\nwashi can also lend a very \"traditional Japanese culture\" vibe to samurai\nwarriors, sumo wrestlers, etc. Some familiar washi users include:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.32405091,
          0.41757143,
          0.88074801,
          0.48098571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.32272871,
          0.41685714,
          0.88207021,
          0.48205714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          36,
          37,
          38,
          39
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日常日语中，washi（我）与老年人及日本西部部分地区的说话习惯联系紧密。在日本娱乐作品里，武士、相扑力士等角色用 washi 自称，还能带出浓厚的“日本传统文化”气息。熟悉的例子包括：",
        "status": "draft",
